#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:106
msgid ""
"User-visible API breaks between v3.8.0 and v3.9.0. Scope: Python C-modules "
"in ``modules/`` and Python libraries in ``scripts/libraries/``."
msgstr ""
"Rotture dell'API visibili all'utente tra la v3.8.0 e la v3.9.0. Ambito: "
"moduli C Python in ``modules/`` e librerie Python in "
"``scripts/libraries/``\\ ."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:109
msgid "Each change is tagged with its impact:"
msgstr "Ogni modifica è contrassegnata dal suo impatto:"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:111
msgid ""
"*major* — affects most scripts that used the feature; you will need to port "
"code."
msgstr ""
"*major* — interessa la maggior parte degli script che usavano la "
"funzionalità; dovrai portare il codice."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:113
msgid "*minor* — narrow API; only affects scripts that used it."
msgstr "*minor* — API ristretta; interessa solo gli script che la usavano."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:114
msgid "*behavior* — same API, different results; re-check tuned scripts."
msgstr ""
"*behavior* — stessa API, risultati diversi; ricontrolla gli script "
"calibrati."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:116
msgid ""
"Changes are grouped by impact in that order. If you just want to port your "
"code, jump to the :ref:`migration checklist <v3_9_0_migration>` at the end. "
"Each commit hash links to its diff on GitHub."
msgstr ""
"Le modifiche sono raggruppate per impatto in quest'ordine. Se vuoi solo "
"portare il tuo codice, vai direttamente alla :ref:`checklist di migrazione "
"<v3_9_0_migration>` in fondo. Ogni hash di commit rimanda al suo diff su "
"GitHub."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:123
msgid "CMSIS-NN ``nn`` module removed *(major)*"
msgstr "Modulo CMSIS-NN ``nn`` rimosso *(major)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:125
msgid ""
"The CMSIS-NN ``nn`` module was removed, including ``nn.load()``, "
"``net.forward()``, ``net.search()``, and the ``nn_class`` helper. Model "
"inference moves to the TensorFlow Lite (``tf``) module. Scripts that loaded "
"``.network`` models with ``nn`` must be ported to ``tf`` with a TensorFlow "
"Lite model."
msgstr ""
"Il modulo CMSIS-NN ``nn`` è stato rimosso, inclusi ``nn.load()``\\ , "
"``net.forward()``\\ , ``net.search()`` e l'helper ``nn_class``\\ . "
"L'inferenza dei modelli passa al modulo TensorFlow Lite (\\ ``tf``\\ ). Gli "
"script che caricavano modelli ``.network`` con ``nn`` devono essere portati "
"a ``tf`` con un modello TensorFlow Lite."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:131
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `fbc767b36 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/fbc767b36>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `fbc767b36 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/fbc767b36>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:136
msgid ""
"``ImageReader`` / ``ImageWriter`` replaced by :class:`image.ImageIO` "
"*(major)*"
msgstr ""
"``ImageReader`` / ``ImageWriter`` sostituiti da :class:`image.ImageIO` "
"*(major)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:138
msgid ""
"``image.ImageReader`` / ``image.ImageWriter`` and their ``next_frame()`` / "
"``add_frame()`` methods were removed and replaced with the new "
":class:`image.ImageIO` type, which supports both memory and file streams via"
" ``read()`` / ``write()`` / ``seek()`` / ``size()`` / ``close()``. Code "
"using the old reader/writer classes must be ported to :class:`image.ImageIO`"
" (see the renamed ``imageio_read.py`` / ``imageio_write.py`` examples)."
msgstr ""
"``image.ImageReader`` / ``image.ImageWriter`` e i loro metodi "
"``next_frame()`` / ``add_frame()`` sono stati rimossi e sostituiti con il "
"nuovo tipo :class:`image.ImageIO`\\ , che supporta sia stream in memoria sia"
" su file tramite ``read()`` / ``write()`` / ``seek()`` / ``size()`` / "
"``close()``\\ . Il codice che usa le vecchie classi reader/writer deve "
"essere portato a :class:`image.ImageIO` (vedi gli esempi rinominati "
"``imageio_read.py`` / ``imageio_write.py``\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:145
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `783a78754 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/783a78754>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `783a78754 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/783a78754>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:150
msgid ":func:`fir.draw_ir` ``scale`` keyword removed *(minor)*"
msgstr "Keyword ``scale`` di :func:`fir.draw_ir` rimossa *(minor)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:152
msgid ""
":func:`fir.draw_ir` was rewritten on top of the new image drawing pipeline. "
"The ``scale=(min, max)`` keyword was removed, and ``hint``, ``x_scale``, "
"``y_scale``, ``roi``, and positional x/y offset arguments were added. "
"Scripts that passed ``scale=(min, max)`` to :func:`fir.draw_ir` must drop it"
" and use the new arguments."
msgstr ""
":func:`fir.draw_ir` è stata riscritta sopra la nuova pipeline di disegno "
"delle immagini. La keyword ``scale=(min, max)`` è stata rimossa, e sono "
"stati aggiunti ``hint``\\ , ``x_scale``\\ , ``y_scale``\\ , ``roi`` e gli "
"argomenti posizionali di offset x/y. Gli script che passavano ``scale=(min, "
"max)`` a :func:`fir.draw_ir` devono eliminarla e usare i nuovi argomenti."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:158
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `0a29103b1 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/0a29103b1>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `0a29103b1 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/0a29103b1>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:163
msgid "``find_lines()`` approximation *(behavior)*"
msgstr "Approssimazione di ``find_lines()`` *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:165
msgid ""
"``image.find_lines()`` now approximates gradient magnitude as ``(abs(gx) + "
"abs(gy)) / 2`` and skips magnitudes below 126. This is faster but changes "
"the set of detected lines and accumulator values, so re-check and re-tune "
"``threshold`` / ``theta_margin`` / ``rho_margin``."
msgstr ""
"``image.find_lines()`` approssima ora la magnitudo del gradiente come "
"``(abs(gx) + abs(gy)) / 2`` e salta le magnitudo inferiori a 126. È più "
"veloce ma cambia l'insieme delle linee rilevate e i valori "
"dell'accumulatore, quindi ricontrolla e ricalibra ``threshold`` / "
"``theta_margin`` / ``rho_margin``\\ ."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:170
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `902ae3c98 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/902ae3c98>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `902ae3c98 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/902ae3c98>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:175
msgid ":func:`fir.snapshot` reworked *(behavior)*"
msgstr ":func:`fir.snapshot` rielaborata *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:177
msgid ""
":func:`fir.snapshot` was substantially reworked with a new keyword API "
"(``hmirror``, ``vflip``, ``transpose``, ``x_scale``, ``y_scale``, "
"``x_size``, ``y_size``, ``scale``, ``rgb_channel``, ``alpha``, "
"``color_palette``, ``hint``, ``pixformat``, ``copy_to_fb``), and the bundled"
" examples were rewritten. The previous positional/``pixformat``-only "
"behavior changed; port FIR scripts to the new keyword form (see the updated "
"thermopile-shield examples)."
msgstr ""
":func:`fir.snapshot` è stata sostanzialmente rielaborata con una nuova API a"
" keyword (\\ ``hmirror``\\ , ``vflip``\\ , ``transpose``\\ , ``x_scale``\\ ,"
" ``y_scale``\\ , ``x_size``\\ , ``y_size``\\ , ``scale``\\ , "
"``rgb_channel``\\ , ``alpha``\\ , ``color_palette``\\ , ``hint``\\ , "
"``pixformat``\\ , ``copy_to_fb``\\ ), e gli esempi inclusi sono stati "
"riscritti. Il precedente comportamento posizionale / solo-\\ ``pixformat`` è"
" cambiato; porta gli script FIR alla nuova forma a keyword (vedi gli esempi "
"aggiornati dello shield termopila)."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:185
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `53f2248b8 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/53f2248b8>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `53f2248b8 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/53f2248b8>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:190
msgid ":func:`fir.init` raises on failure *(behavior)*"
msgstr ""
":func:`fir.init` solleva un'eccezione in caso di fallimento *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:192
msgid ""
":func:`fir.init` now raises (and cleanly de-inits) when the thermal sensor "
"is not detected, instead of silently continuing. Wrap :func:`fir.init` in "
"``try`` / ``except`` (or ensure the sensor is connected) where you "
"previously relied on it not raising."
msgstr ""
":func:`fir.init` solleva ora un'eccezione (e de-inizializza in modo pulito) "
"quando il sensore termico non viene rilevato, invece di proseguire "
"silenziosamente. Avvolgi :func:`fir.init` in ``try`` / ``except`` (o "
"assicurati che il sensore sia connesso) dove prima ti affidavi al fatto che "
"non sollevasse eccezioni."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:197
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `4b2f972f3 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/4b2f972f3>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `4b2f972f3 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/4b2f972f3>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:202
msgid "Migration checklist"
msgstr "Checklist di migrazione"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:204
msgid "For a clean port to v3.9.0 the typical work is:"
msgstr "Per un porting pulito alla v3.9.0 il lavoro tipico è:"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:206
msgid ""
"Port CMSIS-NN ``nn`` model inference to the TensorFlow Lite ``tf`` module "
"(:ref:`the nn removal <v3_9_0_nn>`)."
msgstr ""
"Portare l'inferenza dei modelli CMSIS-NN ``nn`` al modulo TensorFlow Lite "
"``tf`` (\\ :ref:`la rimozione di nn <v3_9_0_nn>`\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:208
msgid ""
"Replace ``image.ImageReader`` / ``image.ImageWriter`` with "
":class:`image.ImageIO` (:ref:`the ImageIO change <v3_9_0_imageio>`)."
msgstr ""
"Sostituire ``image.ImageReader`` / ``image.ImageWriter`` con "
":class:`image.ImageIO` (\\ :ref:`la modifica di ImageIO <v3_9_0_imageio>`\\ "
")."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:210
msgid ""
"Drop the ``scale=(min, max)`` keyword from :func:`fir.draw_ir` and use the "
"new arguments (:ref:`the draw_ir change <v3_9_0_fir_draw_ir>`)."
msgstr ""
"Eliminare la keyword ``scale=(min, max)`` da :func:`fir.draw_ir` e usare i "
"nuovi argomenti (\\ :ref:`la modifica di draw_ir <v3_9_0_fir_draw_ir>`\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:212
msgid ""
"Re-tune ``find_lines()`` parameters against the approximate magnitude metric"
" (:ref:`the find_lines change <v3_9_0_find_lines>`)."
msgstr ""
"Ricalibrare i parametri di ``find_lines()`` rispetto alla metrica di "
"magnitudo approssimata (\\ :ref:`la modifica di find_lines "
"<v3_9_0_find_lines>`\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:214
msgid ""
"Port FIR scripts to the new :func:`fir.snapshot` keyword API (:ref:`the "
"fir.snapshot change <v3_9_0_fir_snapshot>`) and handle :func:`fir.init` "
"raising on a missing sensor (:ref:`the fir.init change <v3_9_0_fir_init>`)."
msgstr ""
"Portare gli script FIR alla nuova API a keyword di :func:`fir.snapshot` (\\ "
":ref:`la modifica di fir.snapshot <v3_9_0_fir_snapshot>`\\ ) e gestire "
":func:`fir.init` che solleva un'eccezione in caso di sensore mancante (\\ "
":ref:`la modifica di fir.init <v3_9_0_fir_init>`\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:219
msgid "All other scripts run unchanged."
msgstr "Tutti gli altri script funzionano senza modifiche."
